{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-156055",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both $x+3<4$ and $3-2x\\le 9$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $x+3<4\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+3 & <4 \\\\ x+3-3 & <4-3 \\\\ x & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/c20ffc0279a42a429797f42fcd929fb4dfb499e311dd3ed7b6b61fd95729953c.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $3-2x\\le 9\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-2x & \\le 9 \\\\ 3-2x-3 & \\le 9-3 \\\\ -2x & \\le 6 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2x) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\ 2x & \\ge -6 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\ge \\frac{-6}{2} \\\\ x & \\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/ae72342a32ea8a952a3d00aec7a8ccc381804ae4b593ba58113911c4bc4b2c09.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/b7d4814919a8c0b2a2ed8e130c8af2bdce5e7fd2d23d10e50e4e293d88170c2f.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $x\\in [-3,1).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
